infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Buffer vs stream: where the body lives
  desc Same response, two memory profiles under a slow client
  compares
    - label Buffer the whole body
      children
        - label Build full response in RAM
          desc Set Content-Length, then send it
        - label Simple, no flow-control logic
          desc One write, nothing to honor
        - label 400 MB body = 400 MB resident
          desc Per concurrent download
        - label OK for small bodies only
          desc Cost scales with body size
    - label Stream with backpressure
      children
        - label Write pieces as they are ready
          desc Transfer-Encoding chunked, size unknown up front
        - label Memory stays flat ~ 16 KB
          desc Bounded by the high-water mark
        - label Stop on false, resume on drain
          desc Production matches the consumer rate
        - label Scales to any body size
          desc pipeline(source, res) is the safe default
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
